    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d114">

                <pb facs="d114-01" n="1" xml:id="d114-01"/>

                <head>114. Notes of Telephone Conversation Between the President’s Assistant for
                    National Security Affairs (Kissinger) and Secretary of State Rogers<anchor n="1" xml:id="d114-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d114-f2"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1969-09-05T12:15:00-04:00">September 5, 1969, 12:15 p.m.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>
                    Rogers said he discussed the seabeds with
                    Mel. They are satisfied but they want to put something in the body that the
                    Soviets and we agree on 3-mile matter for other purposes or some such language.
                    We can’t put it in the body but could footnote it. K said he talked to Mel and under these conditions we should go
                    ahead.</p>
                <p>[Omitted here is discussion unrelated to seabeds.]</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d114-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d114-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Library of Congress, Manuscript Division, Kissinger Papers, Box 360, Telephone Conversations,
                    Chronological File, 1–18 September 1969. No classification marking.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d114-f2" n="2" xml:id="d114-f2-content">
                <p>
                    Kissinger and Rogers discussed the 3 versus 12–mile issue.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
